## Arguments Reference

The following arguments are supported:

As per developer guide: (https://developer.sailpoint.com/docs/api/v3/create-password-policy)

* `name` - (Required) Password policy name.

* `description` - (Optional) Password policy description.

* `source_ids` - (Optional) List of IDs of the sources the policy applies to.

* `default_policy` - (Optional) Whether this is the default password policy.

* `min_length` - (Optional) Minimum password length.

* `max_length` - (Optional) Maximum password length.

* `min_alpha` - (Optional) Minimum number of letters in the password.

* `min_lower` - (Optional) Minimum number of lowercase characters.

* `min_upper` - (Optional) Minimum number of uppercase characters.

* `min_numeric` - (Optional) Minimum number of digits.

* `min_special` - (Optional) Minimum number of special characters.

* `min_character_types` - (Optional) Minimum number of character types the password must contain.

* `max_repeated_chars` - (Optional) Maximum number of repeated characters.

* `use_history` - (Optional) Number of previous passwords that can't be reused.

* `use_dictionary` - (Optional) Whether words in the password dictionary of the tenant are prevented.

* `use_account_attributes` - (Optional) Whether the use of account attributes in the password is prevented.

* `use_identity_attributes` - (Optional) Whether the use of identity attributes in the password is prevented.

* `validate_against_account_id` - (Optional) Whether fragments of the account ID are disallowed in the password.

* `account_id_min_word_length` - (Optional) Minimum length of the account ID fragments that are disallowed.

* `validate_against_account_name` - (Optional) Whether fragments of the account name are disallowed in the password.

* `account_name_min_word_length` - (Optional) Minimum length of the display name fragments that are disallowed.

* `enable_password_expiration` - (Optional) Whether passwords expire.

* `password_expiration` - (Optional) Number of days after which the password expires.

* `first_expiration_reminder` - (Optional) Number of days before expiration when the first reminder is sent.

* `require_strong_authn` - (Optional) Whether strong authentication is required.

* `require_strong_auth_off_network` - (Optional) Whether strong authentication is required off network.

* `require_strong_auth_untrusted_geographies` - (Optional) Whether strong authentication is required from untrusted geographies.

## Attributes Reference

In addition to the Arguments listed above - the following Attributes are exported:

* `id` - Password policy ID.

* `date_created` - The date and time the password policy was created.

* `last_updated` - The date and time the password policy was last updated.

* `connected_services` - Sources the password policy is connected to. Each element contains `id`, `external_id`, `name`, `supports_password_set_date` and `app_count`.

